IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er2-claims`

-- Tests of er2-claims (regulations 25 to 28). Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the regulation named beside it
-- and was decided before the run. One #ASSERT per line.
-- Calendar facts used: 4 March 2026 is a Wednesday (so its week runs Sunday 1 March to Saturday 7 March); 25 December 2026 is a Friday.

§ `Regulation 25 - week of benefits`

#ASSERT `reg 25(2) the percentage of benefits paid for a week` (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 200, 400) EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `reg 25(2) the percentage of benefits paid for a week` (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 400, 400) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `reg 25(2) the percentage of benefits paid for a week` (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 400, 0) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1): one week of benefits each time the total reaches 100
#ASSERT `reg 25(1) the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant is considered to have been paid` (LIST (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 400, 400)) EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `reg 25(1) the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant is considered to have been paid` (LIST (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 200, 400), (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 200, 400)) EQUALS JUST 1
-- 100 + 50 = 150: one week (fork F6)
#ASSERT `reg 25(1) the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant is considered to have been paid` (LIST (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 400, 400), (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 200, 400)) EQUALS JUST 1
-- 100 + 100 + 25 = 225: two weeks
#ASSERT `reg 25(1) the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant is considered to have been paid` (LIST (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 400, 400), (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 400, 400), (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 100, 400)) EQUALS JUST 2
-- 99.75 is not yet 100
#ASSERT `reg 25(1) the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant is considered to have been paid` (LIST (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 399, 400)) EQUALS JUST 0
-- 50 + 50 across different rates: 300 / 600 + 150 / 300 = 100
#ASSERT `reg 25(1) the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant is considered to have been paid` (LIST (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 300, 600), (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 150, 300)) EQUALS JUST 1
-- a week whose rate is not above zero: the text gives no percentage
#ASSERT `reg 25(1) the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant is considered to have been paid` (LIST (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 400, 400), (`er2 Week of benefits paid` OF 100, 0)) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 25.1 - election`

#ASSERT     `reg 25.1 the election referred to in subsection 152.09(1) of the Act is made as required` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25.1 the election referred to in subsection 152.09(1) of the Act is made as required` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25.1 the election referred to in subsection 152.09(1) of the Act is made as required` FALSE TRUE)

§ `Regulation 26 - when a claim for a week must be made`

-- args: a day in the week claimed, consecutive weeks before with no claim
-- Wed 4 Mar 2026: the week ends Sat 7 Mar. (1): three weeks after is 7 Mar + 21 = 28 Mar. (2): one week after is 14 Mar.
#ASSERT `reg 26 the last day for making the claim for a week of unemployment` (YMD 2026 3 4) 0 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 28
#ASSERT `reg 26 the last day for making the claim for a week of unemployment` (YMD 2026 3 4) 3 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 28
#ASSERT `reg 26 the last day for making the claim for a week of unemployment` (YMD 2026 3 4) 4 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 14
#ASSERT `reg 26 the last day for making the claim for a week of unemployment` (YMD 2026 3 4) 10 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 14
-- the Sunday and the Saturday of the same week give the same answer
#ASSERT `reg 26 the last day for making the claim for a week of unemployment` (YMD 2026 3 1) 0 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 28
#ASSERT `reg 26 the last day for making the claim for a week of unemployment` (YMD 2026 3 7) 0 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 28
-- in time on the last day, late on the day after
#ASSERT     `reg 26 the claim for a week of unemployment is made in time` (YMD 2026 3 4) 0 (YMD 2026 3 28)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26 the claim for a week of unemployment is made in time` (YMD 2026 3 4) 0 (YMD 2026 3 29))
#ASSERT     `reg 26 the claim for a week of unemployment is made in time` (YMD 2026 3 4) 4 (YMD 2026 3 14)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26 the claim for a week of unemployment is made in time` (YMD 2026 3 4) 4 (YMD 2026 3 15))
-- a claim that is late under (2) would have been in time under (1)
#ASSERT     `reg 26 the claim for a week of unemployment is made in time` (YMD 2026 3 4) 3 (YMD 2026 3 20)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26 the claim for a week of unemployment is made in time` (YMD 2026 3 4) 4 (YMD 2026 3 20))

§ `Regulation 26.1 - claimants who need not make periodic claims`

#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(1) condition of entitlement to benefits` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(1) condition of entitlement to benefits` FALSE)

-- "period of eligibility": args: reason, apprenticeship (s 25), work-sharing (s 24), the period fixed by the Act, days of the waiting period not yet served
`er2 test fixed period` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 2 1), (YMD 2026 7 4)
`er2 test fixed period plus a week` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 2 1), (YMD 2026 7 11)
-- (a): the waiting period not yet served is added; if it has been served nothing is added
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(1) the period of eligibility` `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE `er2 test fixed period` 7 EQUALS JUST `er2 test fixed period plus a week`
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(1) the period of eligibility` `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE `er2 test fixed period` 0 EQUALS JUST `er2 test fixed period`
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(1) the period of eligibility` `care or support of a critically ill adult` FALSE FALSE `er2 test fixed period` 7 EQUALS JUST `er2 test fixed period plus a week`
-- (b), (c): the period of attendance or of work-sharing employment, without the waiting period
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(1) the period of eligibility` `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` TRUE FALSE `er2 test fixed period` 7 EQUALS JUST `er2 test fixed period`
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(1) the period of eligibility` `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` FALSE TRUE `er2 test fixed period` 7 EQUALS JUST `er2 test fixed period`
-- sickness (12(3)(c)) and regular benefits have no "period of eligibility" in this definition
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(1) the period of eligibility` `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` FALSE FALSE `er2 test fixed period` 7 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(1) the period of eligibility` `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` FALSE FALSE `er2 test fixed period` 7 EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2)(a)
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(a) the claim is an initial claim or one to which subsection 26(2) applies` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(a) the claim is an initial claim or one to which subsection 26(2) applies` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(2)(a) the claim is an initial claim or one to which subsection 26(2) applies` FALSE FALSE)
-- (2)(b): the period of eligibility ends AFTER June 26, 1999
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(b) the claimant's period of eligibility ends after June 26, 1999` (YMD 1999 6 27)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(2)(b) the claimant's period of eligibility ends after June 26, 1999` (YMD 1999 6 26))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(2)(b) the claimant's period of eligibility ends after June 26, 1999` (YMD 1999 6 25))
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(b) the claimant's period of eligibility ends after June 26, 1999` (YMD 2026 7 4)
-- (2)(c)(i): paragraphs 12(3)(a), (b), (d), (e), (f) of the Act; NOT (c), sickness
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(c)(i) the benefits are for a reason set out in paragraph 12(3)(a), (b), (d), (e) or (f) of the Act` `pregnancy`
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(c)(i) the benefits are for a reason set out in paragraph 12(3)(a), (b), (d), (e) or (f) of the Act` `caring for a new-born or adopted child`
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(c)(i) the benefits are for a reason set out in paragraph 12(3)(a), (b), (d), (e) or (f) of the Act` `care or support of a family member`
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(c)(i) the benefits are for a reason set out in paragraph 12(3)(a), (b), (d), (e) or (f) of the Act` `care or support of a critically ill child`
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(c)(i) the benefits are for a reason set out in paragraph 12(3)(a), (b), (d), (e) or (f) of the Act` `care or support of a critically ill adult`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(2)(c)(i) the benefits are for a reason set out in paragraph 12(3)(a), (b), (d), (e) or (f) of the Act` `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(2)(c)(i) the benefits are for a reason set out in paragraph 12(3)(a), (b), (d), (e) or (f) of the Act` `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`)
-- (2)(c): args: reason, apprenticeship, work-sharing, claims for every week
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(c) the claimant makes a claim for every week of unemployment in the period of eligibility, for a reason in (i), under section 25 or under section 24` `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(2)(c) the claimant makes a claim for every week of unemployment in the period of eligibility, for a reason in (i), under section 25 or under section 24` `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(2)(c) the claimant makes a claim for every week of unemployment in the period of eligibility, for a reason in (i), under section 25 or under section 24` `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(c) the claimant makes a claim for every week of unemployment in the period of eligibility, for a reason in (i), under section 25 or under section 24` `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(c) the claimant makes a claim for every week of unemployment in the period of eligibility, for a reason in (i), under section 25 or under section 24` `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- (2)(d): args: completes the Commission's form, states (i), states (ii), states (iii)
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(d) the claimant completes the Commission's form stating (i), (ii) and (iii)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(2)(d) the claimant completes the Commission's form stating (i), (ii) and (iii)` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(2)(d) the claimant completes the Commission's form stating (i), (ii) and (iii)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(2)(d) the claimant completes the Commission's form stating (i), (ii) and (iii)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(2)(d) the claimant completes the Commission's form stating (i), (ii) and (iii)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (2)(d)(ii): args: ceases to meet a condition, that has the effect of reducing or eliminating benefits, has earnings deductible
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(d)(ii) the claimant must notify the Commission as soon as possible` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(2)(d)(ii) the claimant must notify the Commission as soon as possible` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(2)(d)(ii) the claimant must notify the Commission as soon as possible` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(d)(ii) the claimant must notify the Commission as soon as possible` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(2)(d)(ii) the claimant must notify the Commission as soon as possible` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- (2)(d)(iii): at the end of the period of eligibility
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(2)(d)(iii) the day at the end of the period of eligibility on which the claimant must notify the Commission` `er2 test fixed period` EQUALS YMD 2026 7 4
-- (3): ceases to apply "as of the date" the Commission becomes aware: the day before it still applies, that day does not (fork F8)
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(3) section 26.1 still applies to the claim on the day` NOTHING (YMD 2026 5 10)
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1(3) section 26.1 still applies to the claim on the day` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 10)) (YMD 2026 5 9)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(3) section 26.1 still applies to the claim on the day` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 10)) (YMD 2026 5 10))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(3) section 26.1 still applies to the claim on the day` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 10)) (YMD 2026 5 11))

-- the whole exemption: args: initial claim, claim under 26(2), last day of the period of eligibility, reason, apprenticeship, work-sharing,
-- claims every week, completes the form, states (i), (ii), (iii), day the Commission becomes aware (if any), the day in question
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1 the claimant is not required to make periodic claims on the day` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 4) `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- a claim to which 26(2) applies, instead of the initial claim
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1 the claimant is not required to make periodic claims on the day` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 7 4) `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- (a) fails: an ordinary periodic claim
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1 the claimant is not required to make periodic claims on the day` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 4) `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- (b) fails: the period of eligibility ended on 26 June 1999
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1 the claimant is not required to make periodic claims on the day` TRUE FALSE (YMD 1999 6 26) `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 1999 3 1))
-- (c) fails: sickness benefits are not in the list
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1 the claimant is not required to make periodic claims on the day` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 4) `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- (c) fails: no claim for every week
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1 the claimant is not required to make periodic claims on the day` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 4) `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- (d) fails: no form, or the form leaves out (ii)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1 the claimant is not required to make periodic claims on the day` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 4) `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1 the claimant is not required to make periodic claims on the day` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 4) `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- (3): the Commission became aware on 10 Feb 2026, before the day in question: no longer exempt; became aware later: still exempt
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1 the claimant is not required to make periodic claims on the day` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 4) `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 2 10)) (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1 the claimant is not required to make periodic claims on the day` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 4) `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 5 10)) (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- an apprenticeship claim (a reason other than those in 12(3), under section 25) is also exempt
#ASSERT     `reg 26.1 the claimant is not required to make periodic claims on the day` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 4) `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 3 1)

§ `Regulation 27 - persons with mental disabilities, incapacitated persons and deceased persons`

#ASSERT     `reg 27(1) payment of the benefits must be authorized to the person acting on behalf of the claimant` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(1) payment of the benefits must be authorized to the person acting on behalf of the claimant` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(1) payment of the benefits must be authorized to the person acting on behalf of the claimant` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT     `reg 27(2) payment of the benefits must be authorized to the legal representative of the deceased person` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2) payment of the benefits must be authorized to the legal representative of the deceased person` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2) payment of the benefits must be authorized to the legal representative of the deceased person` FALSE TRUE)
-- (3): the executor or the administrator
#ASSERT     `reg 27(3) legal representative` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT     `reg 27(3) legal representative` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(3) legal representative` FALSE FALSE)
-- (4): args: intestate, not worth obtaining letters of administration, not worth obtaining probate
#ASSERT     `reg 27(4) the total value of the estate of the deceased person is not sufficient to warrant obtaining a grant` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(4) the total value of the estate of the deceased person is not sufficient to warrant obtaining a grant` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT     `reg 27(4) the total value of the estate of the deceased person is not sufficient to warrant obtaining a grant` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(4) the total value of the estate of the deceased person is not sufficient to warrant obtaining a grant` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `reg 27(4) the person may make a claim for benefits notwithstanding subsection (2)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(4) the person may make a claim for benefits notwithstanding subsection (2)` FALSE)
-- (4): args: entitled to succeed, estate too small to warrant a grant, claim made under (5), claim made under (6)
#ASSERT     `reg 27(4) the benefits are payable to the person entitled to succeed to the property of the deceased person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(4) the benefits are payable to the person entitled to succeed to the property of the deceased person` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(4) the benefits are payable to the person entitled to succeed to the property of the deceased person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(4) the benefits are payable to the person entitled to succeed to the property of the deceased person` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(4) the benefits are payable to the person entitled to succeed to the property of the deceased person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (5): on the Commission's form, with the declaration and the undertaking
#ASSERT     `reg 27(5) the claim for benefits is made on the form and includes the declaration and the undertaking` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(5) the claim for benefits is made on the form and includes the declaration and the undertaking` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(5) the claim for benefits is made on the form and includes the declaration and the undertaking` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(5) the claim for benefits is made on the form and includes the declaration and the undertaking` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (6): args: a will exists, copy submitted, other persons entitled, release submitted
#ASSERT     `reg 27(6) the applicant submits the copy of the will, if one exists, and the release signed by all other persons entitled to succeed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(6) the applicant submits the copy of the will, if one exists, and the release signed by all other persons entitled to succeed` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT     `reg 27(6) the applicant submits the copy of the will, if one exists, and the release signed by all other persons entitled to succeed` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(6) the applicant submits the copy of the will, if one exists, and the release signed by all other persons entitled to succeed` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `reg 27(6) the applicant submits the copy of the will, if one exists, and the release signed by all other persons entitled to succeed` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT     `reg 27(6) the applicant submits the copy of the will, if one exists, and the release signed by all other persons entitled to succeed` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Regulation 28 - payments in advance`

-- (b)(i), 2026: Christmas is Friday 25 December, in the week Sunday 20 to Saturday 26 December; the week before is 13 to 19 December
#ASSERT     `reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2026 12 25)
#ASSERT     `reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2026 12 20)
#ASSERT     `reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2026 12 26)
#ASSERT     `reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2026 12 19)
#ASSERT     `reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2026 12 13)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2026 12 12))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2026 12 27))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2026 12 29))
-- 2027: Christmas is Saturday 25 December, the last day of the week Sunday 19 to Saturday 25
#ASSERT     `reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2027 12 25)
#ASSERT     `reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2027 12 18)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2027 12 26))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2027 12 11))
-- 2025: Christmas is Thursday; the week of Sunday 28 December 2025 to Saturday 3 January 2026 is two weeks after, and does not count
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2025 12 28))
#ASSERT     `reg 28(b)(i) the week is the week in which Christmas Day falls or the week that precedes it` (YMD 2025 12 21)
-- args: natural disaster, a day in the week, apprenticeship, disruption of services
#ASSERT     `reg 28 the Commission may pay benefits for the week of unemployment in advance of the customary time` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 4) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT     `reg 28 the Commission may pay benefits for the week of unemployment in advance of the customary time` FALSE (YMD 2026 12 22) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT     `reg 28 the Commission may pay benefits for the week of unemployment in advance of the customary time` FALSE (YMD 2026 3 4) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT     `reg 28 the Commission may pay benefits for the week of unemployment in advance of the customary time` FALSE (YMD 2026 3 4) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28 the Commission may pay benefits for the week of unemployment in advance of the customary time` FALSE (YMD 2026 3 4) FALSE FALSE)
